WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:04.259
Considering it’s practically the biggest
movie franchise in history, it can be pretty

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:07.980
hard to keep track of what's going on in the
MCU—and what's coming up.

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:12.460
And while Marvel’s next phases are still
shrouded in secrecy, we do know a few of the

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:14.520
upcoming projects slated for release.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:19.280
In early 2018, writer/director James Gunn
confirmed that the third installment of the

00:00:19.289 --> 00:00:24.181
ridiculously successful Guardians of the Galaxy
franchise would be on its way in 2020, and

00:00:24.181 --> 00:00:28.020
a few months later, he announced via Twitter
that a script had been completed.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:32.300
But an unexpected turn of events threatened
to kill the film entirely: amid a kerfuffle

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:36.630
over some years-old, highly inappropriate
tweets made by Gunn, Disney decided to part

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:37.720
ways with the director.

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:41.880
It was heartbreaking news for fans, not to
mention the cast, who uniformly stood behind

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:43.280
Gunn in a joint public statement.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:47.100
Eventually, it was reported that the House
of Mouse were to use Gunn's script, but would

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.600
not bring him back as director.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:53.320
Luckily for Guardians fans everywhere, Disney
announced in March 2019 that Gunn would be

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:57.160
rejoining the Marvel universe after all, for
Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3.

00:00:57.350 --> 00:01:01.220
Unfortunately, the whole firing scandal means
the project’s release date — which was

00:01:01.239 --> 00:01:06.049
originally set for 2020 — is now up in the
air, but that seems a small price to pay for

00:01:06.049 --> 00:01:08.459
Gunn’s triumphant return to the director’s
chair.

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:10.480
"Boom!"

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:14.960
He may have been last seen crumbling to dust
in the arms of Tony Stark at the end of Avengers:

00:01:14.979 --> 00:01:18.840
Infinity War, but the drama of that moment
was tempered slightly by the fact that we

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:22.660
all knew Tom Holland's Peter Parker would
be back to web-sling another day.

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:26.720
It was known well in advance of the character's
dusting that Holland would be appearing in

00:01:26.729 --> 00:01:31.459
more than one Spidey solo film, and sure enough,
it was later confirmed that Spider-Man: Far

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:34.320
from Home would take place after the events
of Avengers: Endgame.

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:38.649
This sequel will see young Parker going on
a European excursion with his classmates — a

00:01:38.649 --> 00:01:43.399
relaxing sojourn which turns not-so-relaxing
when Nick Fury and Maria Hill show up to enlist

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:46.520
him in the fight against a team of mysterious
elemental monsters.

00:01:47.109 --> 00:01:51.399
Joining the cast is Jake Gyllenhaal as Mysterio,
a longtime Spider-Man nemesis in the comics

00:01:51.399 --> 00:01:54.939
who — if the trailer is to be believed — is
actually fighting on the side of the good

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:56.660
guys... at first, at least.

00:01:56.860 --> 00:02:00.999
But fans know that Mysterio is prone to whipping
up all manner of intricate illusions in support

00:02:00.999 --> 00:02:05.130
of his criminal schemes, so there’s a good
chance there may be more to his relationship

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:07.160
to Spidey’s new foes than meets the eye.

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:12.500
Scarlett Johansson's Black Widow has popped
up in no fewer than six MCU films, and has

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:16.700
exactly the kind of shady past that would
be ripe for further exploration, should Marvel

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:17.840
choose to go that route.

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:21.599
And although a Black Widow solo flick has
been rumored for years, it has finally been

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.720
confirmed that we're actually going to get
one.

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:28.020
The film got the green light in mid-2018,
and Marvel has already begun filling out its

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:28.520
team.

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:32.740
Writer Jac Schaeffer was hired before the
project was even greenlit, and after meeting

00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:37.640
with over 70 potential directors, the studio
finally settled on Australian filmmaker Cate

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:38.140
Shortland.

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:42.840
Shortland's filmography isn’t exactly extensive;
she's perhaps best known for 2012's Lore,

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:45.660
a little-seen but critically acclaimed historical
drama.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:49.620
But if there's one thing we know about Marvel,
it's that their out-of-left-field directorial

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:53.220
choices nearly always turn out to be blindingly
brilliant in hindsight.

00:02:53.569 --> 00:02:57.760
For now, fans can be assured that the project
is in good hands — and all they can reasonably

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:00.951
ask is that Schaeffer and Shortland clue us
in as to what really happened in Budapest.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:04.900
"This is just like Budapest all over again."

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:07.880
"You and I remember Budapest very differently."

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:11.980
With 2016's Doctor Strange a smash hit and
the character playing such a crucial role

00:03:11.989 --> 00:03:16.019
in the conflict with Thanos, it seemed like
a no-brainer that the Sorcerer Supreme would

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:18.300
play a major role in the MCU’s fourth phase.

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:22.340
An unconfirmed report citing an anonymous
source from the Mirror suggests that Benedict

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:26.799
Cumberbatch has received a huge pay bump to
star in the sequel, which may start shooting

00:03:26.799 --> 00:03:31.340
as soon as 2019 — but whether or not this
is actually correct, the inevitability of

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:35.860
Doctor Strange 2 has been confirmed not only
by Cumberbatch, but by Kevin Feige as well.

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:39.579
When asked about continuing in the role by
Deadline, Cumberbatch didn't mince words.

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:40.799
He told the publication:

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:42.240
"Just try to stop me.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:44.740
That's all kind of lined up as far as I'm
aware, but who knows?

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:48.020
I mean, you know, the problem is, how does
he get out of where he's at.

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:49.080
But that's the only thing."

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:53.000
And while doing press for Ant-Man and the
Wasp, Feige confirmed to CinemaBlend that

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:56.440
Doctor Strange 2 would be set a number of
years after the first.

00:03:56.790 --> 00:04:00.860
In December 2018, Hollywood Reporter even
confirmed that Doctor Strange director Scott

00:04:00.879 --> 00:04:04.989
Derrickson would return to helm the project
— but of course, we're not likely to get

00:04:04.989 --> 00:04:08.860
many more details about Doctor Strange 2 until
after Phase Three is complete.

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:13.900
While a sequel based around the Sorcerer Supreme
hasn't been officially confirmed, Marvel isn't

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:16.980
playing nearly as coy about King T'Challa's
second solo outing.

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:21.130
It doesn't have an official title or release
date, but Black Panther 2 has been officially

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:25.389
confirmed by the studio — which isn’t
exactly a huge surprise, considering the original

00:04:25.389 --> 00:04:29.280
became one of the highest-grossing films of
all time and Marvel's first film to receive

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:31.420
a Best Picture nomination at the Oscars.

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:35.420
Not only is the sequel officially happening,
but Feige revealed to Entertainment Weekly

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:37.700
that the concept is already coming together
nicely.

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:38.420
He said:

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:42.760
"One of the favorite pastimes at Marvel Studios
is sitting around on a Part One and talking

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:44.980
and dreaming about what we would do in a Part
Two.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:48.520
There have been plenty of those conversations
as we were putting together the first Black

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:49.080
Panther.

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:53.630
We have ideas and a pretty solid direction
on where we want to head with the second one."

00:04:53.630 --> 00:04:57.830
Writer/director Ryan Coogler is officially
on board, and while nothing is confirmed,

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:02.250
it's expected that the principal cast — including
Chadwick Boseman, Lupita Nyong'O and Danai

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:04.120
Gurira — will also return.

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:08.919
It's even been rumored that Michael B. Jordan's
Erik Killmonger could return in some capacity,

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:12.200
despite being left in no condition to do so
at the end of Black Panther.

00:05:12.430 --> 00:05:15.840
In light of the megabucks that film made,
we're likely to get additional details on

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:18.840
this highly-anticipated sequel sooner rather
than later.

